description:
We are looking for a bright and enthusiastic Accounts Assistant, providing support to the Assistant Accountant / Client Legal Cashier to ensure accurate financial records in the firm's multi-books for the London and Europe LLP's, and perform various financial and tax related duties.

The role also works closely with the Billing and Accounts Payable teams, and the wider business to ensure compliance with the SRA Solicitors Accounts Rules.

This law firm has an international network across 20 office locations and employs over 1000 lawyers. They have recently moved to amazing new offices that are ideally situated for a number of stations including Liverpool Street, Fenchurch Street or Cannon Street.

Responsibilities
- Complete bank reconciliations for office and client accounts;
- Complete balance sheet reconciliations for specified accounts and follow up on reconciling items on a timely basis
- Prepare accounting journal entries in the firm's multi-books.
- Assist in the preparation of VAT returns.
- Assist in the preparation of annual financial statements under UK Financial Reporting Standards.
- Support the statutory audit process by collating documentation as needed and liaising with auditors;
- Preparation of other financial and tax analyses as needed.
- Arrange client account payments and office to client account payments under the supervision of the Legal Cashier;
- Processing quarterly interest due on client accounts;
- Assist with the annual SRA Solicitors Accounts Rules audit;
- Completing monthly and quarterly Office of National Statistics returns;
- Provide backup for the Accounts Payable function during peak times and absences as required;
- Assist with new accounting system implementations, including user acceptance testing and training.
- Other ad hoc duties as required;

Candidate Profile
- A-level or equivalent;
- At least one year's experience in the accounts department of a law firm or other professional service organisation;
- IT literate. Comfortable with using Microsoft Excel and generative AI tools
- Aderant Client Management System experience an advantage, but not essential;

Important Notice

It is Career Legal's policy, as a matter of courtesy, to respond to all applications within three working days. However because of the volume of applications, we are sometimes unable to respond to individual candidates. If we have not contacted you within three working days your application has been unsuccessful and your details have not been retained. Please apply for any other position that you may see in the future. Thank you.

